hadiths[1]{hadithnumber,text}:
"1333","Al-Hasan bin Muhammad narrated to us, Affan narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, Hisham bin Urwa narrated to us, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Aisha, that Saad He was thrown on his ankle, so the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, made a tent for him in the mosque to bring him back soon. He said: Then his words to Al-Banru’ became stifled, so he said: “ Oh God, you know that there is no one more beloved to me than striving for you than people who denied your prophet, expelled him, and did and did, and I think If war has broken out between us and them, then break out this speech so that my death will be in it. He said: So one night he was among them when his speech broke out. Then blood flowed from his wound until he entered the people’s tent, so they called out: O people of the tent, what is this that is coming to us from before you? So they looked and, lo, “His heart exploded at his words, and behold, his blood was rushing.”"
